WEBVTT

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>GUNDAM</i>

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>MOBILE SUIT</i>

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:17.870
<i>hoshi ga furishikiru penthouse de
In the penthouse that watches the stars fall...</i>

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:24.040
<i>sora no ORUGO-RU hitori kiiteta
I listened to Heaven's music box...</i>

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:30.460
<i>GARASU no RO-PU wo mekakushi de wataru
Walking, blindfolded, across a tight-rope of glass...</i>

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:37.090
<i>minna sabishii SA-KASU no kodomo sa
Everyone is like, the lonely child of the circus.</i>

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:45.020
<i>hitori bocchi no kanashimi ni
The rope that creaks with the sadness of isolation...</i>

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.770
<i>kishinda tsuna ga kokoro de yureteru...
...is still locked deep in my heart...</i>

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:07.830
<i>yasashii me wo shita dareka ni aitai
I wish to meet the one who's eyes glow with warmth!</i>

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:25.980
<i>sasayaite kureyo soba ni iruyotte Silent Voice
Whisper to me that you'll always be there by my side, Silent Voice.</i>

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:37.350
Fa came to tell us
Kamille had disappeared,

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:41.930
so we all went to look for him.
That was when Arius attacked!

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:45.610
Ple tried her best, but she can't fight
in machines she's not used to.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:48.280
But then, we heard a voice.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:50.570
The voice of God, guiding us.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:53.120
At least, that's how
it sounded to us.

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:58.580
FALLING SKY

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.940
You're getting a message
from the Audhumla?

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:14.390
From Hayato?

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:16.770
I can't quite process it on
the communications monitor,

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:18.980
but it seems to be approaching
pretty close to us.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:21.190
A message from
the Audhumla?

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:24.410
Are the Minovsky particles
around here that thin?

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.190
What?!

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:29.110
What's the meaning of this,
Hayato? What's happened?!

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:31.570
I'll give you the
details when I get there!

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:34.250
Just get the Argama
back to Dublin!

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.910
I want to save as many
as I can before it falls!

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.080
Before what falls?

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:42.680
A colony! One of Side 4's
colonies is falling!

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:46.510
They're doing a colony drop?

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:49.060
A colony's dropping on Earth?

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.900
Kamille! Calm down, Kamille!

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:11.780
You're safe here! Relax!

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.070
Kamille!

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:15.820
Ple, are you okay?

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:18.410
Ever since I heard about the
colony dropping onto Dublin,

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.630
I've been wondering
if you felt sick.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.380
l can handle it, but...

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:28.010
Judau.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.890
Kamille can sense it, can't he?

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:37.680
Just the ship changing course wouldn't
cause this much pain for him.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:38.890
What's happened?

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:41.100
A colony's falling on Dublin.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.810
The Argama's going to assist in
rescue operations before it does.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:47.780
No! If we go there, what's going
to happen to Kamille?!

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:16.140
At last, you're dropping the colony.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:18.810
The objective of
this colony drop...

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:21.390
isn't merely to cause
destruction to the surface.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:25.520
The terror it brings will
demonstrate our power!

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.480
If we don't show that no
one can resist our power,

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.190
there's no point in having it!

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:32.030
If we leave them
even a bit of hope,

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:34.610
people will once again
rise against us!

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:36.490
Lady Haman.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:40.290
I give my word that I shall
live up to your expectations!

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:42.250
Is Dublin clearing?

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:45.710
I see.
Amuro's gone into space?

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:48.040
If he was here,
we might have been able...

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.930
to hold back the
Federation government.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:54.510
So even though Haman's dropping
this colony out of impatience,

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:57.390
all we can do is sit on
our hands and watch.

00:04:57.390 --> 00:05:00.810
She's trying to crush the AEUG's
influence in one blow here.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.980
To cut off our movements
through an act of terror.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.100
It's unforgivable!

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:11.480
When you consider what an effect
death has on other people, then...

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:15.610
Hayato.
This was Katz's room.

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:18.120
We've remodeled
a lot since he was here...

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.880
But we left this room as it was.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:37.600
We put his other things in storage
before we entered Earth's gravity.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:48.240
If I had just tried harder, then...

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.810
You saw him die?

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:50.780
Yes.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.110
I heard about it before, but...

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:57.950
But I need to tell Fraw and
the kids about it, don't I?

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:03.340
When Kamille recovers, he can
tell you about how Katz died.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:07.240
Kamille? I'd like to see Kamille.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:10.180
I'll see how he is.
Hang on.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:23.480
That's strange...
Fa should be there.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:25.730
Bright?

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:29.270
Dammit, Beecha, get the hatch open
before the captain finds out!

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:31.100
Kamille's resisting!

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:31.960
Judau!

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:32.900
Captain!

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.770
This is an emergency!
What are you doing?!

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:36.490
Going out, sir!

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.900
Stop!

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:42.070
Captain Bright,
l asked Judau to do this.

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:46.920
He's worried about Kamille.
He mustn't go to Dublin!

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:48.620
Kamille...!

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:51.370
Please, drop them off in Glasgow.

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:55.210
At this rate, if he goes to a place
where a colony's falling, Kamille will be...!

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:58.130
The Argama isn't going to slow
down so you can stop in Glasgow!

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:02.010
Isn't stopping the colony drop
a job for the Earth Federation?

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:03.890
Why does the Karaba or
the AEUG have to do it?!

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:05.970
Because the Earth
Federation government...

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:08.390
knows it's happening and
won't do anything!

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:09.680
What do you mean?

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.690
The government elite
would do anything...

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:14.730
to decrease the population
by even a single person!

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:19.230
Less mouths to feed, huh?
These aren't rats we're talking about!

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:21.110
So don't go running off
over your personal feelings!

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:23.070
Kamille was a pilot!

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:23.700
Out!

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:25.120
Hayato!

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:27.370
Kamille!

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:28.500
Oh, boy.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:29.910
He ran away!

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:31.170
Kamille!

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:34.380
Not so rough!

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:35.500
I know!

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:35.920
Kamille.

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:39.880
See? Even now, Kamille's
desperate enough to fight.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:43.240
If you were on White Base,
you should at least see that!

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:46.180
Stop it, Judau. That's enough.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:47.730
Enough...

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:01.910
Katz...

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:08.050
You're forcing Kamille to get
caught up in this fight, mister!

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.580
We don't have a plane
to spare for Kamille now!

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:11.870
Captain!

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:14.590
He can use the plane I flew here.

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:16.500
Hayato...

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:18.560
I'll go back
aboard the Dodai.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:21.130
Judau, I'll expect you
to work extra hard for this.

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:21.940
Fa!

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:24.420
Good ol' White Base crew!

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.890
We did it!

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:27.850
Thank you, Hayato.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:29.760
Just hurry.

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:31.980
We can put Kamille on this!

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:33.890
Whoa, good idea!

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:35.270
There we go...

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:38.200
Move it!
We're passing by Glasgow!

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.690
Hayato, thank you.

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:44.570
No, Kamille is...

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:46.280
Go on, Kamille.

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:48.410
Get in, please, Kamille.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:50.290
Leave this to us!

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:51.540
Right.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:05.900
Kamille, you just...

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:07.060
Ju...

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:17.450
I'll contact you later.

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:20.070
Judau!

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:23.690
Just now, I...

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:25.990
Yeah. I saw it, too.

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:28.890
I... I kinda saw something.

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:31.990
Kamille was trying
to tell us something.

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:34.000
But what was it?

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:37.250
Those kids might understand.

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:39.510
I envy them.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:48.890
Kamille...

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:52.180
I think your feelings got
through to those kids.

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:54.610
It's okay. Don't worry.

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:32.270
When did you pick up this ship
over England en route to Dublin?

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:35.560
Since the report was made by phone,
and accounting for instrument error,

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:38.070
it was less than an hour ago!

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:44.520
These new Zaku IIIs will end the
AEUG's rescue efforts in failure!

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:48.410
Let's go! Close all roads
leading out of Dublin!

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:54.700
Dreissen unit, go on ahead!

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:55.710
Roger!

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:05.510
Rakan Dahkaran, moving out!

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:12.890
Now, you decrepit denizens
of the Earth Federation...

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:16.680
Now to teach you the
meaning of the word despair.

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:18.650
Lady Haman...

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:27.610
We're receiving a
TV broadcast from Dublin.

00:11:27.610 --> 00:11:28.480
TV?

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:29.900
Yes, sir.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:34.780
It's still unclear how long we have
until the colony falls onto Dublin.

00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:37.540
As the Federation government
denies the truth of this matter,

00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:39.290
rescue operations
are late in starting!

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:41.790
Roads in town are still
completely jammed.

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:44.090
The rescue team from
the Karaba is currently...

00:11:56.030 --> 00:11:58.780
Close all roads out of the city!

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:02.110
Leave as many rats for
the colony as you can!

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:18.540
I think I saw
Kamille's heart, as well.

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:24.210
It was full of
sad things, wasn't it?

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:29.760
Yeah. Which is why
I have to stop this.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:33.510
Yeah. That's right.

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:38.100
So, I'll be leaving you alone
for a while, but be strong for me.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:40.680
I understand.

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:41.690
What?

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:44.490
l love you.

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:48.440
Ple...

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:53.400
Do your best, in my place. Don't let
Kamille's feelings be wiped away.

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:57.870
Don't worry. Now go to sleep
and let your wounds heal.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:11.380
How's the sea rescue going?
The enemy's attacking from the land.

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:13.590
The boats are taking them out,
but the process is slow.

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:15.640
Then speed it up!
How about air-cargo planes?

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:18.640
The colony hits in four hours!

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:22.390
The waves it'll cause will be huge!
Work like we have three hours!

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:23.980
Argama, are you ready?

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:26.440
We're launching all
our carrier-based planes.

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:27.980
You'll have command!

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:30.480
There are apparently enemies
hiding near the airport, as well!

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:32.400
Leave it to us.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:35.400
Drop the containers!
Cover Judau and the others!

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:36.290
Aye, sir!

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:39.870
Core fighter!
Judau Ashta, moving out!

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:45.300
Core Top!
Elle Vianno, moving out!

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:50.800
Core Base!
Iino Abbav, moving out!

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:58.680
Even if we start right now...!

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:02.770
Cut the chatter! There's no telling
when the enemy will show up!

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:09.690
Dodai unit will pick up
the refugees at the airport.

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:12.940
I want to save every last person
we can before time runs out!

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:16.490
I want Federation
collaborators saved, as well!

00:14:16.490 --> 00:14:19.500
They have proof of
the Federation's betrayal!

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:26.080
Please, no pushing!

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.010
Stay in line!
We'll get going soon!

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:34.300
Hey, can we carry that many?

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:36.880
We'll just have to try, won't we?

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:40.910
No pushing! There are Dodais coming,
too! There's plenty of room!

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:42.650
To the south!

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:53.560
Multiple enemy contacts,
bearing southwest at 25 km!

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:55.480
Beecha! Mondo! Let's go!

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:56.190
Roger!

00:14:56.190 --> 00:14:57.940
Judau, you and the others,
stand by here!

00:14:58.190 --> 00:14:59.410
Roger!

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:06.790
Arrival of flight 125
for Glasgow is delayed.

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:08.790
But we have tickets!

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:10.790
There's an emergency in Dublin.

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:13.800
Their flights have priority.
Please bear with us.

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:19.430
Kamille, it'll be a
while longer...

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:28.480
Judau!

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:32.310
Kamille! We have to
wait a little bit longer.

00:15:32.310 --> 00:15:35.070
It looks like all the flights
through Dublin are packed.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:55.970
What's that light?

00:15:57.230 --> 00:15:58.880
How could they?!

00:15:58.880 --> 00:16:01.590
A ship full of evacuees
has been destroyed!

00:16:01.590 --> 00:16:02.600
What?!

00:16:03.740 --> 00:16:05.550
How much longer?!

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:07.310
Pardon me.

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:08.890
l was here first!

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:12.690
We have a reservation.
Minister, just sign here.

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:16.980
Those fools in the Karaba are going
to be wiped out by resisting Haman.

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:20.280
Once the AEUG's back is broken,
the war will be over.

00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:24.160
We should have given Side 3
to Haman from the start.

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:28.200
At least this'll bring down the
price of food a bit here on Earth.

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:31.210
Hey! Don't say that out loud!

00:16:35.350 --> 00:16:36.880
Kamille!

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:45.020
The sky...
The sky is falling!

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:51.890
Beecha, he's running your way!
We'll squeeze him!

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:53.030
Roger!

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:56.980
Roux, we're launching
the heavies! Don't get hit!

00:16:56.980 --> 00:16:59.030
Triple missiles, fire!

00:17:04.630 --> 00:17:07.910
Enemy mobile suits moving
from the coast into Dublin!

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:10.630
Right! Launch Dodais!

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:19.220
You're not getting
into town that easy!

00:17:23.340 --> 00:17:25.180
I've got more!

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:39.110
The AEUG have gotten into the airport!
Concentrate on them!

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:43.330
I'm not letting you
get away with this!

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:45.200
Damn Karaba!

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:54.460
You think that'll work?!

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:58.630
Damn! That pilot's good!

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:04.360
Trying to pincer me, huh?

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:06.880
Jump off and
buy us some time!

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:09.390
We'll destroy the airport
in the meantime!

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:10.440
Roger!

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:14.180
Come on! I can take
you both out if I self-destruct!

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:18.110
Katz, I might be able
to hear your voice...

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:20.240
Don't!

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:28.650
Why are you stopping me?!
If we don't slow them down,

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:30.410
they'll destroy the Audhumla!

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:33.450
Because it's normal to stop a guy
in front of you from killing himself!

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:39.500
How long till
the estimated time?

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:41.580
We're down to an hour!

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:43.880
This will be our last pickup.

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:47.430
Can Judau and the others hold
them off on their own till then?

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:51.640
Roux!
Get yourselves out of there!

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:53.100
But there are still enemies!

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:54.810
They're running for it!

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:58.100
If we delay any longer,
we'll be flattened by the colony, too!

00:18:58.100 --> 00:19:00.190
Judau's team is surrounded
by the enemy!

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:01.200
Judau!

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:08.200
Ignore the ones in front!
The ship further in is the target!

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:11.660
The Audhumla!

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:16.580
Iino! Elle! We're gonna dock
and form the Double Zeta!

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:17.500
Dock?!

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:18.500
Here?!

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:20.210
It's now or never!

00:19:20.210 --> 00:19:21.670
That light!

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:28.010
If we form the Double Zeta,
three suits will be no problem!

00:19:28.010 --> 00:19:29.350
Judau!

00:19:31.530 --> 00:19:32.810
No!

00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:35.690
What?!

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:39.480
Hayato!

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:42.990
Oh, no!

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:02.880
Dammit! This plane won't
do what I tell it to!

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:07.130
Is that you I hear, Katz...?

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:09.510
Hayato!

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.480
Why?!

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:29.740
Judau, are you okay?!

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:35.750
Why can't we all
just live together?!

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:36.820
Judau!

00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:41.130
Oh, no. The sky will fall...!

00:20:42.830 --> 00:20:46.430
No! If they cause
any more grief, then...!

00:21:11.190 --> 00:21:13.860
Judau! The colony will
land any moment now!

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:15.910
Get away from Dublin at once!

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:18.280
I still haven't shot
that mobile suit down!

00:21:18.280 --> 00:21:18.990
We're going back!

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:19.990
We don't wanna die!

00:21:19.990 --> 00:21:23.290
No! Not until
I've shot him down!

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:24.870
Beecha, get out of there!

00:21:24.870 --> 00:21:27.010
I know, but the Double Zeta is...!

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:29.260
Here he comes!

00:21:33.860 --> 00:21:36.340
You haven't run yet?!
Are you mad?!

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:39.140
How can you fight a war
and not be mad?!

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:15.310
At last...

00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:50.820
<i>ikuyaku ikuman ikuoku no hoshi yo
Hundreds upon thousands upon millions of stars...</i>

00:22:50.820 --> 00:22:56.950
<i>naze hikaru dake nano ka kataru chikara no shiwase
...why do you just sit there and twinkle? Show me the power that lets me connect!</i>

00:22:56.950 --> 00:23:08.050
<i>Ima nara ore demo furikaerasu ni tobitatsu kokoro
For now, even I've got a mind that wanders without reminiscing past regrets!</i>

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:13.930
<i>Hoshi no kazu dake inochi wo takuwareba
If lives are really stored in the form of stars...</i>

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:19.940
<i>ginga no mure no hikari wo kaete misero
...show me how to change the light and move galaxies...</i>

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:29.650
<i>kono te ga tsukamu inochi no omosa ni naru
The weight of life itself, will be held in my hands!</i>

00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:35.530
<i>mada meinai yo sora no michishirude wa
Space's guidepost is still not within my sights...</i>

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:41.620
<i>kono te ni saware hikari isenmanen
Let the light of 10 million years touch this hand!</i>

00:23:46.350 --> 00:23:51.000
The colony may have fallen on Dublin,
but there's no time to be mad about it.

00:23:51.000 --> 00:23:55.000
Because Glemy, hoping to redeem
himself, has released Ple-Two.

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:58.470
I'm not sure what that means,
but Ple seems to know.

00:23:58.470 --> 00:24:00.760
And while we're horrified
by this gigantic monster...

00:24:01.010 --> 00:24:04.050
Ple! What are you
doing out here?!

00:24:04.050 --> 00:24:07.930
Next time, on Gundam ZZ:
"Prisoner of Gravity: Ple-Two."

00:24:04.810 --> 00:24:07.930
Next Time

00:24:04.810 --> 00:24:07.930
PRISONER OF GRAVITY: PLE-TWO

00:24:08.570 --> 00:24:10.310
How much worse can this get?!
